### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim is refuted because the scientific evidence consistently shows that face masks **reduce** but do not **stop** the spread of COVID-19. The WHO Director-General explicitly stated that "[m]asks alone will not protect you from COVID-19," a pre-October 2020 systematic review found only modest reductions in transmission (~6% in community settings, ~19% in households), and a laboratory study by Kim et al. concluded that even fully sealed N95 masks "were not able to completely block the transmission of virus droplets/aerosols" ([Kim et al., 2020](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33087517/); [systematic review](https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.1101/2020.04.01.20049528v1)). The epidemiological literature uniformly uses language of "reducing risk" rather than complete prevention—a meta-analysis reported an odds ratio of 0.38 (a ~62% reduction), not elimination ([PubMed PMID 33347937](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33347937/)). The claim's absolute language overstates the evidence. Additionally, the attribution is questionable: Yinon Weiss's article titled "These 12 Graphs Show Mask Mandates Do Nothing to Stop COVID" appears to refute rather than assert this position, suggesting the claim may have been misattributed or extracted as a straw-man argument from the [original Federalist article](https://thefederalist.com/2020/10/29/these-12-graphs-show-mask-mandates-do-nothing-to-stop-covid/).